[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.8,2.8);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, above left] {$b$};
\draw (B) -- (C);
\pic[draw, "$45^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=B--A--C};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The area of $\Delta ABC$ is $28\text{ cm}^{2}$. Find the length of side $b$, correct to $1$ decimal place.

