[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (A) at (2.9,2.6);
\draw (C) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$15\text{ cm}$};
\draw (C) -- (A) node[midway, above left] {$13\text{ cm}$};
\draw (A) -- (B);
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=B--C--A};
\node[below left] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (A) {$A$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The area of $\Delta ABC$ is $65\text{ cm}^{2}$ and $\theta$ is an acute angle. Find $\theta$, correct to $1$ decimal place.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (4,0);
\coordinate (R) at (-1.5,2.0);
\draw (P) -- (Q) node[midway, below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (P) -- (R) node[midway, above right] {$5\text{ m}$};
\draw (R) -- (Q);
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=Q--P--R};
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above left] at (R) {$R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The area of $\Delta PQR$ is $16\text{ m}^{2}$ and $\angle QPR = \theta$ is obtuse. Find $\theta$, correct to $1$ decimal place.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate, decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt) -- (0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (3.5,0);
\coordinate (B) at (-1.2,3.3);
\draw[tickmark] (V) -- (A) node[midway, below] {$x$};
\draw[tickmark] (V) -- (B) node[midway, above right] {$x$};
\draw (A) -- (B);
\pic[draw, "$110^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=A--V--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The isosceles triangle has an area of $32\text{ m}^{2}$. Find the length $x$ of each equal side, correct to $2$ decimal places.
